  "term": "collaborative filtering",
  "definition": "Collaborative filtering is a personalized recommendation method that uses a person’s past behavior or queries and compares them with similar users to suggest relevant items. In the source, it is described as a way to recommend research articles while adapting recommendations based on user similarity and changes in interests over time.",
